  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1209 PM CDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nBreezy southwesterly winds will abate around sunset early this\nevening. Another chilly night is anticipated as clear skies and\nlight winds allow temperatures to drop into the mid-to-upper 30s\nand low 40s overnight, outside of the warmer Chicago metro \narea. Patchy frost may develop towards morning in the coldest \nlocations; however, another Frost Advisory is not planned. \n\nFollowing Monday's cool start, sunny skies and lighter winds \nwill allow temperatures to warm quickly through the morning, \nreaching highs in the mid-to-upper 60s, with a few low 70s \npossible south of I-80. Dry and unseasonably mild weather will \npersist for the foreseeable future as high pressure dominates \nacross the Great Lakes. This will bring an extended stretch of \npleasant late October weather, with daily highs ranging from the\nupper 60s to mid-70s (slightly cooler near the lake) under \nmostly sunny skies. While these temperatures are well above \naverage for late October (around 60 degrees), they remain \ncomfortably below record highs in the mid-to-upper 80s.\n\nKJB",
